WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
A tree falls in a forest
and lies on the ground,

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.460
year after year.

3
00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:09.880
Under the bark, fine threads of
fungus are growing through the wood.

4
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.130
Wood is full of cellulose:
large molecules,

5
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.550
built from many sugar units.

6
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.430
Slowly, the log gets softer
and smaller, until it is gone.

7
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.620
So how does a fungus, with
no mouth and no stomach,

8
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.120
digest a fallen tree?

9
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.700
In this mission, you'll zoom in on the tip
of one fungal thread as it grows through

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.780
the wood.

11
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.960
Then you'll follow a
dog's meal in four stages,

12
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.730
from the first bite to new muscle.

13
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out how a fungus digests
a tree with no mouth and no stomach.
